      "html": "† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">בַּרְזִלַּי</span></big>  <strong>nome próprio masculino (</strong><em>homem de ferro</em>; não há adjetivo derivado de nomes de metais; talvez aramaico, e <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּר</span> = <em>filho</em>, Nes<sup>ZPV xv. 257; AJSL, Apr. 1897, 173</sup><strong>) </strong><br><strong>1.</strong>  um gileadita <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 17:27\" href=\"/II_Samuel.17.27\">2Sm 17.27</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 19:32\" href=\"/II_Samuel.19.32\">2Sm 19.32</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 19:33\" href=\"/II_Samuel.19.33\">2Sm 19.33</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 19:35\" href=\"/II_Samuel.19.35\">2Sm 19.35</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 19:40\" href=\"/II_Samuel.19.40\">2Sm 19.40</a> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 2:7\" href=\"/I_Kings.2.7\">1Rs 2.7</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּרְזִלָּי֑</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 19:34\" href=\"/II_Samuel.19.34\">2Sm 19.34</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezra 2:61\" href=\"/Ezra.2.61\">Ed 2.61</a> = <span data-ref=\"Nehemiah 7:62\" data-bdbh-source-href=\"/Nehemiah.7.62\" data-bdbh-suspended=\"BIBLE_LABEL_TARGET_MISMATCH\">Ne 7.63</span> <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּנֵי בַרְזִלַּי אֲשֶׁר לָקַח מִבְּנוֹת בַּרְזִלַּי הַגִּלְעָדִי וַיִּקָּרֵא עַל־שְׁמָם</span>, onde o segundo Barzilai é o acima mencionado, e o primeiro é<br><strong>2.</strong>  um sacerdote <a data-ref=\"Ezra 2:61\" href=\"/Ezra.2.61\">Ed 2.61</a> = <span data-ref=\"Nehemiah 7:62\" data-bdbh-source-href=\"/Nehemiah.7.62\" data-bdbh-suspended=\"BIBLE_LABEL_TARGET_MISMATCH\">Ne 7.63</span>, que adotou o nome <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּרְזִלַּי</span>.<br><strong>3.</strong>  <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 21:8\" href=\"/II_Samuel.21.8\">2Sm 21.8</a> um meolatita.",
